## Pricing & Billing

The system will include a flexible pricing engine to automatically calculate the transport price for each trip.

Pricing should be configurable through user-defined business rules rather than hardcoded logic.

Potential pricing factors include:

- Fixed prices
- Customer-specific pricing
- Route-based pricing
- Pickup and delivery locations
- Terminal-specific pricing
- Vehicle type
- Trailer type
- Container type
- Combination trips
- Waiting time
- Additional stops
- Weekend or holiday surcharges
- Ferry or toll costs
- Manual adjustments
- Custom pricing rules

The pricing engine should remain fully configurable so that pricing logic can evolve without requiring major changes to the application.

Future functionality may include:

- Rule-based pricing configuration
- Price simulations
- Automatic invoice preparation
- Cost analysis
- Profit margin calculations
- Historical pricing reports
- Customer-specific pricing profiles

---

## Communication

The platform will include a communication module to simplify interaction with drivers and customers.

The communication layer should remain extensible and support multiple communication channels.

Potential capabilities include:

- Sending trip information
- Sending PDF transport orders
- Sending loading instructions
- Sending container information
- Sending updated planning
- Sending route changes
- Receiving documents from drivers
- Receiving photos
- Receiving signed documents
- Receiving proof of delivery (POD)
- Receiving container numbers
- Receiving notes from drivers

Future communication channels may include:

- WhatsApp Business
- Email
- SMS
- Push notifications
- Mobile application
- Other messaging platforms

The communication module should be independent from the transport planning module, allowing additional communication providers to be integrated in the future.

